Do not cache an lstat miss: a file created after the miss stays missing.

`PosixSourceAccessor::cachedLstat` (src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc)
keeps every lstat result in one static map for the whole process, misses
included, and nothing but `invalidateCache` of that path drops an entry.
`nix` the command evaluates once and exits. A process that evaluates for
days does not: havsorm's salt-master workers looked for a pillar file at
minion start, before it was written, and no later EvalState in those
processes saw it until the master restarted (nixidae/nixidae#903,
nixidae/nixidae#940). Measured in one process: miss, write the file, a
fresh EvalState still says "does not exist".

A hit stays cached, as before: an edit is read through `readFile`, which
does not use this cache. A miss costs one lstat each time. 2.35 replaced
this cache with directory file descriptors and caches no stat, so the
patch is 2.34's only.

diff -ruN a/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc b/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc
--- a/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc	2026-10-21 03:58:05.937328174 +0200
+++ b/src/libutil/posix-source-accessor.cc	2026-10-21 03:58:27.389483837 +0200
@@ -83,6 +83,12 @@
 
     auto st = nix::maybeLstat(absPath.c_str());
 
+    /* A miss is not cached: the cache is process-wide, and a path that
+       is created after its first lookup would stay missing for every
+       evaluator after. */
+    if (!st)
+        return st;
+
     if (cache.size() >= 16384)
         cache.clear();
     cache.emplace(std::move(absPath), st);
